      "source": {
        "kind": "shine"
      },
      "question": "Read the extract and answer the questions.\n\n*If ever you should go by chance*\n*To jungles in the East;*\n*And if there should to you advance*\n*A large and tawny beast,*\n\n(i) Which animal is being described?\n\n(ii) What does 'tawny' mean?\n\n(iii) How will you recognise it, according to the poem?\n\n(iv) Name the device in 'there should to you advance'.\n\n(v) What is the tone of the poem?",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "answer_steps": [
        "(i) The Asian Lion.",
        "(ii) Brownish-yellow.",
        "(iii) It roars at you as you are dying.",
        "(iv) Inversion.",
        "(v) Humorous."
      ],
      "marking_scheme": [
        "(i) 1 mark",
        "(ii) 1 mark",
        "(iii) 1 mark",
        "(iv) 1 mark",
        "(v) 1 mark"
      ]
    },
    {
